I've read the roster. It's an ATRIA REGIONAL LHR-based AT72 short-haul month — **all printed times are LOCAL to the station shown**, so I've converted everything: LHR/DUB = BST/IST = UTC+1 all September, and ARN/CDG/FRA/BCN/FCO = CEST = UTC+2. Reporting offset applied is the printed short-haul 40 min (every sector here is short haul; the 70-min long-haul line is unused).

The shape of the month: no nightstops, so your body clock stays on London time throughout — the fatigue risk isn't timezone shift, it's the **whiplash between 05:45 local departures and duties that land at 02:00–03:00 local**, repeatedly, with a single day off in between. That drove the plan below.

